.TH GNUTEMPO 1 "2025" "GNUTempo v1.1.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
gnutempo \- Terminal-based minimalist metronome

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gnutempo
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
GNUTempo is a free, offline, unrestricted terminal-based metronome written in Python. It supports arbitrary time signatures, layered beats with bar synchronization, swing/groove control, and visual pattern editing.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help and exit.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug mode for diagnostic output.

.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bpm \fI<value>\fR
Set starting BPM (default: 120).

.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-time \fI<signature>\fR
Set time signature, e.g., 4/4, 7/8 (default: 4/4).

.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preset \fI<name>\fR
Use preset rhythm pattern. Available presets: rock, jazz, bossa, waltz, funk, samba, triplet, half_time, double_time, seven_eight.

.TP
.BR \-\-test
Run self-tests and exit.

.TP
.BR \-\-list-presets
List all available presets with descriptions.

.TP
.BR \-\-no-sound-check
Skip audio file verification at startup.

.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
Once running, the following commands are available:

.TP
.B mkbt ##/## bpm
Create a beat with specified time signature and tempo.

.TP
.B sync && mkbt ##/## bpm
Create a beat synchronized to the next bar of an existing beat.

.TP
.B p <id>
Pause a beat by ID.

.TP
.B r <id>
Resume a paused beat by ID.

.TP
.B rm <id>
Remove a beat by ID.

.TP
.B lsbt
List all active beats.

.TP
.B sanitize [id | all]
Fix oversized slots in beat patterns.

.TP
.B patui <id>
Open the visual pattern editor for a beat.

.TP
.B swing <id> <value>
Set global swing (-0.5 to 0.5).

.TP
.B swing <id> slot <index> <value>
Set per-slot swing override.

.TP
.B tkmod <1|2>
Switch between hi-fi (1) and low-fi (2) sound sets.

.TP
.B export
Save all beats to a JSON file.

.TP
.B import [index]
Load beats from a JSON file.

.TP
.B lsjsn
List available JSON files.

.TP
.B debug [subcmd]
Access debug/diagnostic tools. Subcommands: on, off, info, timing, audio, state.

.TP
.B tap
Enter tap tempo mode to determine BPM by tapping.

.TP
.B help
Show all interactive commands.

.TP
.B exit / quit
Exit the program.

.SH PRESETS
The following preset rhythms are available:

.PP
.B rock
\- Basic rock pattern (4/4 @ 120 BPM)

.PP
.B jazz
\- Swing pattern (4/4 @ 140 BPM)

.PP
.B bossa
\- Bossa nova pattern (4/4 @ 130 BPM)

.PP
.B waltz
\- Waltz pattern (3/4 @ 90 BPM)

.PP
.B funk
\- Funk pattern with 16th notes (4/4 @ 100 BPM)

.PP
.B samba
\- Samba pattern (2/4 @ 160 BPM)

.PP
.B triplet
\- Triplet feel (4/4 @ 120 BPM)

.PP
.B half_time
\- Half-time rock (4/4 @ 70 BPM)

.PP
.B double_time
\- Double-time punk/metal (4/4 @ 180 BPM)

.PP
.B seven_eight
\- Progressive 7/8 pattern (7/8 @ 140 BPM)

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Start interactive mode
gnutempo

# Quick start with custom settings
gnutempo --bpm 120 --time 4/4

# Start with a preset
gnutempo --preset rock

# Enable debug mode
gnutempo --debug

# Run self-tests
gnutempo --test

# List all presets
gnutempo --list-presets
.fi

.SH PATTERN EDITOR
When using \fBpatui\fR, the following keys are available:

.PP
.B left/right arrows
Move between slots

.PP
.B s
Split a slot (Enter to halve, 1/3 for ratio, =3 for N equal parts)

.PP
.B m
Enter merge mode (expand with arrows, Enter to confirm)

.PP
.B w/W
Nudge slot swing +/- 0.01

.PP
.B g/G
Nudge global swing +/- 0.01

.PP
.B r
Reset selected slot swing

.PP
.B R
Reset all swing to zero

.PP
.B x
Hard reset pattern to equal subdivision

.PP
.B q/ESC
Close editor (changes are live immediately)

.SH REQUIREMENTS
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3.x
.IP \(bu 2
pygame library

.SH FILES
.IP \(bu 2
.I bartick.ogg
\- Bar tick sound (required)
.IP \(bu 2
.I tick.ogg
\- Regular tick sound (required)
.IP \(bu 2
.I lbt.ogg
\- Low-fi bar tick (optional)
.IP \(bu 2
.I ltk.ogg
\- Low-fi tick (optional)
.IP \(bu 2
.I *.json
\- Saved beat patterns

